{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794535008973,"sessionID":"ses_e2d61a612ffeqDQKVegFwIo8rA","part":{"id":"prt_1d29f2acd001JHgXMFUJreCUFw","sessionID":"ses_e2d61a612ffeqDQKVegFwIo8rA","messageID":"msg_1d29f1525001KXBYlFFrYSxDmr","type":"step-start","snapshot":"c6ea50484c3b03f01183bd47f3f91a1e20daf2ea"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794535013541,"sessionID":"ses_e2d61a612ffeqDQKVegFwIo8rA","part":{"partID":"prt_1d29f38de001uJJjKNq72YYEC5","sessionID":"ses_e2d61a612ffeqDQKVegFwIo8rA","messageID":"msg_1d29f1525001KXBYlFFrYSxDmr","type":"tool","id":"call_875f68c43fc24480b5ea1e1e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md, lines 1-92\n1: ---\n2: description: \"Tune and rebuild the skill advisor, and audit graph freshness, router reach, budgets and parent hubs.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write\n5: ---\n6: <!-- skill_agent: system-skill-advisor -->\n7: \n8: # /doctor:skill-advisor Router\n9: \n10: This command is a thin router. It resolves the target and setup values from `_routes.yaml`, then loads the target workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n11: \n12: ### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n13: \n14: **STATUS: BLOCKED** until `target` is bound.\n15: \n16: 1. Parse the first positional token of `$ARGUMENTS` as `target`, before any flag. `list`, `?` and `--list` render the route manifest instead of binding a target, and `--target=<name>` is a compatibility alias.\n17: 2. Treat an absent or whitespace-only target as missing. Do not infer it from conversation history, open files, earlier runs or repository state.\n18: 3. When it is missing, show the presentation contract's target-resolution prompt, stop, and wait. Use only `$ARGUMENTS` or that explicit reply.\n19: \n20: If this gate was skipped, stop, say so, return to it, and bind the target before loading any workflow.\n21: \n22: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n23: \n24: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n25: \n26: Load the presentation contract before showing startup questions, setup dashboards, approval prompts, diagnostic dashboards, result summaries, or next-step text.\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n31: \n32: | Purpose | Asset |\n33: |---------|-------|\n34: | Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n35: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` |\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n40: \n41: - `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest; this command owns the routes whose `command` is `/doctor:skill-advisor`.\n42: - `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`.\n43: - The positional target is parsed before any flag; global flag pre-parse is forbidden.\n44: - Unknown or cross-target flags fail before YAML load.\n45: - The YAML start condition is: target bound, workflow asset exists, presentation asset loaded, and every target setup variable resolved.\n46: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n47: - The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns visible wording and layout.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n52: \n53: These existing YAML assets are referenced only. The router must not modify them.\n54: \n55: | Target | Workflow |\n56: |--------|----------|\n57: | `tune` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` |\n58: | `rebuild` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` |\n59: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` |\n60: | `router-reach` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-router-reach.yaml` |\n61: | `skill-budget` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-budget.yaml` |\n62: | `parent-skill` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-parent-skill.yaml` |\n63: \n64: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`.\n65: 2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and keep the `/doctor:skill-advisor` routes.\n66: 3. Take `target` from the input gate.\n67: 4. If target is unknown, render the presentation contract's unknown-target failure and stop.\n68: 5. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating`, `mcp_tools`, `cli_commands`, and script invocations from the route.\n69: 6. Parse remaining flags using only the resolved target's `allowed_flags`; reject cross-target flags using the presentation contract's error wording.\n70: 7. Resolve any missing setup variables using the presentation contract's per-target setup prompts.\n71: 8. Load the resolved workflow YAML from `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/<yaml>` and execute it step by step.\n72: 9. Use the presentation contract, not this router, for user prompts, dashboards, result summaries, and next-step display.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n77: \n78: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`:\n79: \n80: - Target-resolution menu, help text, accepted answers, and failure wording.\n81: - Per-target setup prompts for unresolved fields.\n82: - Route manifest display for `list`, `?`, or `--list`.\n83: - The rebuild plan, approval prompt and result templates.\n84: - Troubleshooting and next-step display text.\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n89: \n90: The router resolves a `target` against the `/doctor:skill-advisor` routes in `_routes.yaml`, binds that target's workflow YAML plus its setup variables, allowed flags, and mutation class, then executes it step by step under an always-interactive mode.\n91: `tune` re-tunes the scoring lanes with per-skill review, `rebuild` rebuilds `skill-graph.sqlite` through the advisor CLI behind a backup, and the four read-only targets report graph drift, router reach, description budgets and parent-hub structure.\n92: `list`, `?`, or `--list` render the route manifest instead of dispatching.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md, lines 1-92\n1: ---\n2: description: \"Tune and rebuild the skill advisor, and audit graph freshness, router reach, budgets and parent hubs.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Bash, Grep, Glob, Edit, Write\n5: ---\n6: <!-- skill_agent: system-skill-advisor -->\n7: \n8: # /doctor:skill-advisor Router\n9: \n10: This command is a thin router. It resolves the target and setup values from `_routes.yaml`, then loads the target workflow YAML and the presentation contract.\n11: \n12: ### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n13: \n14: **STATUS: BLOCKED** until `target` is bound.\n15: \n16: 1. Parse the first positional token of `$ARGUMENTS` as `target`, before any flag. `list`, `?` and `--list` render the route manifest instead of binding a target, and `--target=<name>` is a compatibility alias.\n17: 2. Treat an absent or whitespace-only target as missing. Do not infer it from conversation history, open files, earlier runs or repository state.\n18: 3. When it is missing, show the presentation contract's target-resolution prompt, stop, and wait. Use only `$ARGUMENTS` or that explicit reply.\n19: \n20: If this gate was skipped, stop, say so, return to it, and bind the target before loading any workflow.\n21: \n22: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n23: \n24: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n25: \n26: Load the presentation contract before showing startup questions, setup dashboards, approval prompts, diagnostic dashboards, result summaries, or next-step text.\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n31: \n32: | Purpose | Asset |\n33: |---------|-------|\n34: | Route manifest | `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` |\n35: | Presentation source of truth | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt` |\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n40: \n41: - `_routes.yaml` is the canonical routing and mutation-class manifest; this command owns the routes whose `command` is `/doctor:skill-advisor`.\n42: - `execution_mode` is always `INTERACTIVE`.\n43: - The positional target is parsed before any flag; global flag pre-parse is forbidden.\n44: - Unknown or cross-target flags fail before YAML load.\n45: - The YAML start condition is: target bound, workflow asset exists, presentation asset loaded, and every target setup variable resolved.\n46: - If any referenced asset is missing, stop and report the missing path.\n47: - The YAML owns workflow behavior; the presentation Markdown owns visible wording and layout.\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n52: \n53: These existing YAML assets are referenced only. The router must not modify them.\n54: \n55: | Target | Workflow |\n56: |--------|----------|\n57: | `tune` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` |\n58: | `rebuild` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` |\n59: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` |\n60: | `router-reach` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-router-reach.yaml` |\n61: | `skill-budget` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-budget.yaml` |\n62: | `parent-skill` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-parent-skill.yaml` |\n63: \n64: 1. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`.\n65: 2. Read `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` and keep the `/doctor:skill-advisor` routes.\n66: 3. Take `target` from the input gate.\n67: 4. If target is unknown, render the presentation contract's unknown-target failure and stop.\n68: 5. Resolve `yaml`, `setup_vars`, `allowed_flags`, `mutating`, `mcp_tools`, `cli_commands`, and script invocations from the route.\n69: 6. Parse remaining flags using only the resolved target's `allowed_flags`; reject cross-target flags using the presentation contract's error wording.\n70: 7. Resolve any missing setup variables using the presentation contract's per-target setup prompts.\n71: 8. Load the resolved workflow YAML from `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/<yaml>` and execute it step by step.\n72: 9. Use the presentation contract, not this router, for user prompts, dashboards, result summaries, and next-step display.\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n77: \n78: The following content lives only in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`:\n79: \n80: - Target-resolution menu, help text, accepted answers, and failure wording.\n81: - Per-target setup prompts for unresolved fields.\n82: - Route manifest display for `list`, `?`, or `--list`.\n83: - The rebuild plan, approval prompt and result templates.\n84: - Troubleshooting and next-step display text.\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n89: \n90: The router resolves a `target` against the `/doctor:skill-advisor` routes in `_routes.yaml`, binds that target's workflow YAML plus its setup variables, allowed flags, and mutation class, then executes it step by step under an always-interactive mode.\n91: `tune` re-tunes the scoring lanes with per-skill review, `rebuild` rebuilds `skill-graph.sqlite` through the advisor CLI behind a backup, and the four read-only targets report graph drift, router reach, description budgets and parent-hub structure.\n92: `list`, `?`, or `--list` render the route manifest instead of dispatching."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794535012574,"end":1794535013541}}}}
