{"type":"text","timestamp":1794535142862,"sessionID":"ses_e2d61a612ffeqDQKVegFwIo8rA","part":{"id":"prt_1d2a1241d0011B8lHPT2FxwpOp","sessionID":"ses_e2d61a612ffeqDQKVegFwIo8rA","messageID":"msg_1d2a11980001iIgu7yE6syt6N1","type":"text","text":"T018 is done. `.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md` now carries the `embedder` target in both places.\n\n**Verify command and output** (run from the repo root, `DOC` = `.skilled/commands/doctor`):\n\n```\n$ rg -n \"embedder\" .skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md\n3:argument-hint: \"<tune|rebuild|skill-graph-freshness|router-reach|embedder|skill-budget|parent-skill> [flags] | list | ?\"\n61:| `embedder` | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml` |\nexit=0\n```\n\nTwo lines, above the required minimum of two.\n\n**Files written:** `.skilled/commands/doctor/skill-advisor.md` only. The scoped diff is two lines, the `argument-hint` alternation and one table row placed after `router-reach`, matching the position the route already holds in `_routes.yaml` at line 227. The row points at `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml`, which I confirmed exists.\n\n**One thing to know, not caused by this edit.** I also ran `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` as a read-only sanity check and it exits 1 with three J1 failures:\n\n```\nFAIL: J1: target-set parity mismatch — missing from skill-advisor presentation menu (Accepted answers): embedder\nFAIL: J1: target-set parity mismatch — missing from skill-advisor presentation 'Valid targets:' line: embedder\nFAIL: J1: target-set parity mismatch — missing from skill-advisor presentation subsystem manifest table: embedder\n```\n\nThose are all in `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt`, which T015 owns and which is still unticked. `route-validate.py:629` also checks the router's own targets table, and that leg no longer appears in the failure list, so this edit closed the router-table half of J1 rather than opening anything. T014's own Verify gate therefore stays red until T015 lands.\n\n**Not done:** the tasks.md checkbox is unticked, as instructed.\n\n**Handback:** nothing is blocked on you for T018. T015 is the remaining unblocker for `route-validate.sh` to exit 0, and it belongs to another worker.","time":{"start":1794535138333,"end":1794535142862}}}
